    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Beach</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A beach is a geographical feature next to a body of water consisting of loose particles. The particles that make up a beach are usually made of rock, such as sand, gravel, pebbles, etc., or from biological sources, such as mollusk shells or coralline algae. Sediments are deposited in different densities and structures, depending on local wave action and climate, creating different textures, colors, and gradients or layers of material.
There&apos;s no better place to escape the stress of everyday life than the beach. You can relax and sunbathe, watch the waves, or even take a nap in a hammock strung between two palm trees. You might even make new friends at the beach!</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Beach</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Beach</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
