        <IRI>#Bus</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A bus is a vehicle designed to transport large numbers of people on urban roads. It is generally used in urban and interurban public transportation services, as well as on fixed-route routes. Its capacity can vary between 10 and 120 passengers. In bus rapid transit systems, bus capacity can vary between 160 and 240 passengers.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
