        <IRI>#Comfort</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The comfort category is identified as three stars within a five-star system. This classification is defined by the corresponding hotel association, which depends on whether the hotel&apos;s country has adopted this standard system.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Comfort</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Comfort_Cathegory</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Company</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A company is understood to be an economic agent where economic factors are efficiently organized to produce goods and services for the market with the aim of achieving certain objectives. That is, a system of human, technical, and financial elements, directed and organized according to a specific hierarchy or organizational structure carried out by a manager or entrepreneur in the exercise of a managerial or entrepreneurial function. In this ontology, it is a company that manages passenger transportation services.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Company</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Company</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Comunidad_Valenciana</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The Valencian Community (officially in Valencian: Comunitat Valenciana) is an autonomous community of Spain located in the east of the Iberian Peninsula. It was formally established in 1982 with the approval of its Statute of Autonomy and, since 2006, has been considered a historical nationality under the provisions of Article 2 of the Constitution.
The current territory of Valencia largely coincides with that of the historic Kingdom of Valencia, which survived from the 13th to the 18th century as part of the Crown of Aragon.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Comunidad_Valenciana</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Valencian_Community</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Comunidad_de_Madrid</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The Community of Madrid is a Spanish autonomous community located inland on the Iberian Peninsula, on the Southern Sub-Plateau of the Central Plateau. It borders the provinces of Ávila and Segovia in Castile and León, as well as Toledo, Guadalajara, and a small part of Cuenca in Castile-La Mancha. The Community of Madrid is a single-province region, so there is no provincial council. Its capital, Madrid, is also the capital of Spain.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Comunidad_de_Madrid</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Community_of_Maddrid</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Concert_Valencia</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A show in which one or more musical compositions are performed, whether indoors or outdoors, and which maintains a certain unity.</Literal>
