    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Rural</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The main characteristic of rural hotels is their location in the heart of nature, surrounded by natural landscapes such as mountains, rivers, forests, or meadows. Furthermore, they are usually designed to offer a more authentic experience, incorporating rustic and local elements.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Rural</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Rural</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#San_Sebastián</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">San Sebastián (officially known in Basque as Donostia) is a city and municipality located on the Cantabrian Sea coast, in the Bay of Biscay, 20 km from the French border. The city is the capital of the province of Guipúzcoa, in the autonomous community of the Basque Country. Its population is 189,093 (INE 2024) and its metropolitan area reaches 436,500 (2010). It is the capital of the Bayonne-San Sebastián Basque Eurocity, a conurbation of more than 620,000 inhabitants.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#San_Sebastián</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">San_Sebastián</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#San_Sebastián_Coords</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Positive latitudes indicates north of the equator, negative latitudes indicate south. Positive longitudes indicate east of the Greenwich Meridian, negative longitudes indicates west.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#San_Sebastián_Coords</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">San_Sebastián_Coords</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Sevilla</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Seville is a municipality and city in Spain, capital of the province of the same name and of Andalusia. With a population of 687,488 inhabitants (INE 2024), it is the most populated city in Andalusia and the fourth in Spain according to official data from the INE. The municipality has an area of ​​141.4 km². The metropolitan area of ​​Seville is made up of 46 municipalities, includes a population of 1,548,741 inhabitants (INE 2020) and occupies an area of ​​4,905.04 km². Seville, having its Royal Alcázar, is one of the four cities where the Spanish royal family has an official residence, along with Madrid, Barcelona and Palma.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Sevilla</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Seville</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
