        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Sevilla_Coords</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Positive latitudes indicates north of the equator, negative latitudes indicate south. Positive longitudes indicate east of the Greenwich Meridian, negative longitudes indicates west.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Sevilla_Coords</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Seville_Coords</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Spain</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Spain, formally the Kingdom of Spain, is a sovereign transcontinental country, constituted as a social and democratic state governed by the rule of law and whose form of government is a parliamentary monarchy. It is one of the 27 sovereign states that make up the European Union. Its territory, with its capital in Madrid, is organized into 17 autonomous communities, each made up of 50 provinces and two autonomous cities.
Spain is located primarily in southwestern Europe..</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:isDefinedBy"/>
        <IRI>#Spain</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spain</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Spain</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Spain</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Sports</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A sporting event is an organized activity that involves physical or mental competition among participants. It can range from a local tournament to an international championship. Its primary objective is the practice or enjoyment of sports, while also promoting values ​​such as teamwork, discipline, and personal improvement.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Sports</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Sport</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Standard</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The standard category is identified as two stars within a five-star system. This classification is defined by the corresponding hotel association, which depends on whether the hotel&apos;s country has adopted this standard system.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Standard</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Standard_Cathegory(2-stars)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Taxi</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A taxi is a fare-regulated mode of transportation consisting of a vehicle with a driver that offers transportation services for one person or a small group of passengers to the same or different destinations, either for a fee or on a contract basis. Pickup and drop-off locations are usually decided by the provider (supplier), while in the case of a taxi, the user (demander) determines them. In other words, unlike other types of passenger transportation, such as metro, tram, or bus lines, taxi services are characterized by being door-to-door. The person whose job is to drive a taxi is called a &quot;taxi driver.&quot;</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Taxi</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Taxi</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Taxi_Barna</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Taxi service in Barcelona.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
