        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Taxi_Barna</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Taxi_Barna</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Taxi_Bilbo</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Taxi service in Bilbao..</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Taxi_Bilbo</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Taxi_Bilbo</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Technological</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A technology conference is an educational event that discusses advances and developments in the fields of technology, regardless of their specialty. They are a meeting place for debate and exposure to a specific technology sector through experiences and knowledge.
Workshops: A speaker explains a concept and provides instructions throughout the workshop so the audience can replicate it. They typically last about two hours.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Technological</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Technological</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Toledo</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Toledo is a Spanish municipality and city, capital of the province of the same name, in the autonomous community of Castilla-La Mancha. With a population of 86,526 (INE 2024), it is the third most populated municipality in the region. The historic center is located on the right bank of the Tagus River, on a hill surrounded by a pronounced meander. The municipal area includes two neighborhoods very separate from the main center: Azucaica, on the right bank of the river, and Santa María de Benquerencia, located practically opposite the former on the left bank.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>#Toledo</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Toledo</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Toledo_Coords</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Positive latitudes indicates north of the equator, negative latitudes indicate south. Positive longitudes indicate east of the Greenwich Meridian, negative longitudes indicates west.</Literal>
