        <Literal xml:lang="en">Zaragoza</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <IRI>#Zaragoza</IRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">Zaragoza is a municipality and city in Spain, capital of the province of the same name and of the autonomous community of Aragon. Belonging to the Central Region, it has a special legal status as the capital of Aragon. It is the fifth most populated municipality in Spain, with a registered population of 686,986 inhabitants (INE 2024), behind Madrid, Barcelona, ​​Valencia, and Seville.
It is located on the banks of the Ebro, Huerva, and Gállego rivers and the Imperial Canal of Aragon, in the central part of the Ebro Valley. Part of its municipal area is occupied by the Sotos y Galachos del Ebro Nature Reserve.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
